WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
If you already have a draft, you've probably read it so many times at this

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.160
point that you don't know if it looks good and you don't know if it's

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.000
actually going to move the needle in a positive direction for you.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.760
That's what these read and edit options are for.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.080
Basically, you will give me a Google doc link to your essay or your essays,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.300
and for each revision, I will send you back feedback within 48 hours.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.920
I got into every college that I applied to, $600,000 in merit

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.960
scholarships and a full tuition scholarship to Vanderbilt because of

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.440
my college essays, and since then, I've worked with over a thousand

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.800
students directly, helping them write amazing essays that have gotten them

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.980
into schools like Penn, UC Berkeley with a Regent Scholarship, Dartmouth,

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.600
NYU, Cornell, and so many others.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.600
And that is the exact strategy that I'm going to be applying

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.680
to your essay as I'm editing it.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.240
So I will tell you what things to add to your essay.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.800
I will reword some things for you if the grammar is off or the sentence

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.160
structure sounds bad, and I will make sure that you know exactly how to

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.400
tighten up each essay of yours so that it stands out and moves the needle

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.040
in a positive direction for you.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.560
It's basically the same amount of expertise and guidance you would

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.480
get on a one-on-one call with me, except you don't have to have

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.520
the hassle of scheduling calls and trying to make time in your busy

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.280
schedule, especially if you're a senior dealing with a lot of things at once.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.320
I offer a one-time edit on a single essay, or you can get packages of

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.440
edits, like multiple edits and revisions on your Common App Essay, multiple

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.440
edits on your supplementals, or I have an option for both.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.520
Alternatively, if you just want one call of guidance with me, then I

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.360
also have a hybrid option where you can just do one call and then

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.680
get written edits after that.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.480
If you feel completely stuck though, like you don't know where to start,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.520
then that's where I would recommend that you book one of

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.520
my live one-on-one call options.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.800
But if you already have stuff prepared and you just want to know if it's

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.920
good and make sure that it is ready to submit and it's going to move

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.880
the needle in a good direction for you, that's exactly what these

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.280
written edits are for, and I would love to help you.
